WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.509 --> 00:00:10.000
For Groomer Books, the biggest pile is the middle one: three hundred and ten minutes a week of work an agent can draft and the founder approves.

2
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.842
Here's how the example week came out, with example numbers.

3
00:00:13.862 --> 00:00:17.692
Twenty-five tasks, seven hundred and sixty minutes.

4
00:00:17.712 --> 00:00:25.214
Agent alone: seven tasks, one hundred and ninety minutes, like researching competitors and sorting receipts.

5
00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:34.633
Agent drafts, you approve: nine tasks, three hundred and ten minutes, including client emails, social posts and invoice reminders.

6
00:00:34.653 --> 00:00:43.761
Only you: nine tasks, two hundred and sixty minutes, like reconciling the bank feed, paying bills and signing a new client.

7
00:00:43.817 --> 00:00:45.459
Notice where money went.

8
00:00:45.479 --> 00:00:49.537
Reconciling the bank feed and paying bills sit in only you.

9
00:00:49.557 --> 00:00:57.944
The first hire is the biggest recurring job in the middle pile: overdue-invoice reminders, seventy-five minutes a week.

10
00:00:57.964 --> 00:01:06.681
The brief gives the agent read access to the invoicing app, lets it draft reminders, and makes it ask before anything sends.

11
00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:09.046
That's your first agent job.

